182
00:21:16,812 --> 00:21:22,113
[SPEAKER_02]: You can't assume that just because you're feeling anxiety, it's necessarily correct.

183
00:21:22,153 --> 00:21:28,835
[SPEAKER_02]: So, what is the basis for me experiencing this anxiety?

184
00:21:30,536 --> 00:21:31,796
[SPEAKER_02]: It has to be based on

185
00:21:34,454 --> 00:21:36,996
[SPEAKER_02]: Recognition of things that you're genuinely liable to.

186
00:21:37,056 --> 00:21:45,023
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, you don't fabricate that sense of anxiety to kind of give yourself a boost of sense of urgency in the practice.

187
00:21:45,824 --> 00:21:47,665
[SPEAKER_00]: It has to be something that is already there.

188
00:21:47,846 --> 00:21:49,347
[SPEAKER_02]: You're not, like, creating it.

189
00:21:50,108 --> 00:21:54,792
[SPEAKER_02]: So, you recognize the things that already are lurking there in your experience.

190
00:21:54,852 --> 00:21:55,092
[SPEAKER_02]: Like,

191
00:21:56,573 --> 00:21:58,074
[SPEAKER_00]: Your own body, you don't know.

192
00:22:00,716 --> 00:22:09,582
[SPEAKER_00]: You have no access to the gears and the mechanism that keep it working.

193
00:22:09,602 --> 00:22:11,144
[SPEAKER_00]: It's how your basic organs function.

194
00:22:11,164 --> 00:22:12,284
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

195
00:22:12,525 --> 00:22:17,568
[SPEAKER_02]: So then, you realize, on that level, that anxiety is

196
00:22:18,629 --> 00:22:22,654
[SPEAKER_02]: The anxiety is in things being a certain way.

197
00:22:22,674 --> 00:22:24,756
[SPEAKER_02]: The anxiety is not something you fabricate.

198
00:22:25,297 --> 00:22:33,426
[SPEAKER_02]: And so, the practice then is, once a person starts to feel that anxiety in that right way,

199
00:22:34,546 --> 00:22:37,547
[SPEAKER_02]: Then, the practice is not to, like, fix the anxiety or resolve it.

200
00:22:38,367 --> 00:22:46,329
[SPEAKER_02]: It's to go through it, so to say, so that that anxiety ceases to cause you suffering.

201
00:22:47,089 --> 00:22:58,371
[SPEAKER_02]: Because, as the Buddha said, like, impermanence, uncertainty, suffering and not-self, these are the characteristics of the aggregates.

202
00:22:58,571 --> 00:23:00,912
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not like... or your entire experience.

203
00:23:01,152 --> 00:23:01,792
[SPEAKER_02]: It's not like...

204
00:23:02,392 --> 00:23:04,473
[SPEAKER_02]: Things are that way only when you're ignorant.

205
00:23:05,474 --> 00:23:15,980
[SPEAKER_02]: So, the fact of the aggregates being suffering, being unsatisfactory, will remain always.

206
00:23:16,580 --> 00:23:29,088
[SPEAKER_00]: Even when you're not ignorant anymore, these things are still anxious, but you are not subject to anxiety anymore, because you're not invested in them anymore.

207
00:23:29,208 --> 00:23:29,728
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, that's right.

208
00:23:33,628 --> 00:23:38,190
[SPEAKER_02]: So, that's how... that's that kind of perpendicular direction.

209
00:23:38,230 --> 00:23:51,276
[SPEAKER_02]: Instead of, like, doing something to the anxiety or covering it up or managing it, you find a way so that it's... it just doesn't... it just doesn't affect you.

210
00:23:51,876 --> 00:23:52,617
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's...

211
00:23:53,657 --> 00:23:54,778
[SPEAKER_00]: I came up with an analogy.

212
00:23:54,818 --> 00:23:59,220
[SPEAKER_00]: It's like you have a bucket or a barrel that's going to be filled with liquid.

213
00:24:00,716 --> 00:24:09,700
[SPEAKER_02]: The solution to freedom from suffering is not to limit the amount of liquid that's going to come in, or the types of liquid that are going to come in.

214
00:24:10,421 --> 00:24:12,742
[SPEAKER_02]: It's to make it so that the barrel has no bottom.

215
00:24:14,123 --> 00:24:21,966
[SPEAKER_02]: So that, basically, there is no type of anxiety that would be capable of overwhelming your mind.

216
00:24:22,547 --> 00:24:22,907
[SPEAKER_00]: Not like

217
00:24:24,082 --> 00:24:27,244
[SPEAKER_00]: The anxiety is limited now, and that's why I don't get overwhelmed.

218
00:24:27,944 --> 00:24:44,693
[SPEAKER_02]: It's... you want to go in the direction of making yourself immovable to any amount of anxiety, let alone... like, you have to overcome not just physical pain and things that can come from other people.

219
00:24:44,713 --> 00:24:52,738
[SPEAKER_00]: It's your own mind, fundamentally, that has these susceptibility to these emotions, the states, and that's what you have to overcome.

220
00:24:54,504 --> 00:25:02,691
[SPEAKER_04]: So, this anxiety is related to a sense of groundlessness, to the point that one has not understood that there will be anxiety.

221
00:25:02,931 --> 00:25:03,732
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah.

222
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:06,875
[SPEAKER_04]: Or, rather, one will be affected by anxiety, which is suffering.

223
00:25:07,115 --> 00:25:07,315
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

224
00:25:08,196 --> 00:25:15,803
[SPEAKER_02]: So, then, anxiety that's not resisted, or anxiety that's properly understood, is not suffering.

225
00:25:16,344 --> 00:25:17,084
[SPEAKER_02]: That's right.

226
00:25:17,325 --> 00:25:19,687
[SPEAKER_02]: It's like, it might feel pessimistic,

227
00:25:20,867 --> 00:25:21,848
[SPEAKER_02]: When you have wrong view.

228
00:25:22,448 --> 00:25:22,648
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

229
00:25:22,768 --> 00:25:27,789
[SPEAKER_02]: But when you understand, then it's just the way things are.

230
00:25:27,949 --> 00:25:28,690
[SPEAKER_02]: It's just realist.

231
00:25:29,410 --> 00:25:35,212
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, you can have the right type of joy and the right type of peace.

