238
00:26:16,028 --> 00:26:18,289
[SPEAKER_04]: So, on one level, there is sort of a buffer.

239
00:26:18,749 --> 00:26:21,270
[SPEAKER_04]: Like, if one doesn't restrain oneself, this is never going to happen.

240
00:26:21,730 --> 00:26:24,572
[SPEAKER_04]: But, one can get sort of caught in this intermediate space.

241
00:26:25,132 --> 00:26:31,375
[SPEAKER_04]: And then, the the way to not be overwhelmed is, in fact, to attend more closely to

242
00:26:32,255 --> 00:26:42,719
[SPEAKER_04]: One's virtue and one's sense restraints, if one doesn't want to practically become overwhelmed by the anxiety that's going to arise, if one moves into the, let's say, genuine authenticity here.

243
00:26:45,600 --> 00:27:01,526
[SPEAKER_03]: Can we say that, like, virtue and sense restraint kind of make one face this anxiety, but, like, progressively, with, like, the right type of basis, instead of, like, just being confronted, like, to the full extent of it, like, at the moment of death, or when one

244
00:27:08,157 --> 00:27:12,579
[SPEAKER_04]: Yeah, because the minds... because if it's done rightly, it will be a training on their minds.

